00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:48,800
And like, I guess we haven't really said exactly what it is, but it's, I mean, basically what you're describing, it's like a digital version of a physical planner app or a planner notebook, right?

112
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:50,240
Yeah, that's right.

113
00:10:50,640 --> 00:11:00,480
We're very inspired by physical planners and notebooks and wanted to bring in lots of decorative elements like to remind you of the paper based planners.

114
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:03,600
That's where I feel like it really, really stands out.

115
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:16,800
Like, I feel like a lot of the, uh, sort of stand out design apps, uh, at least lately, have been sort of like, what if Apple made, you know, XYZ thing?

116
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:24,960
And I feel like you guys went in a very different direction in a way that's really, really kind of interesting, which is kind of running away fromning away from that.

117
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:26,720
It doesn't feel like something that Apple would have made.

118
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:31,120
It feels like something Apple would have made maybe like ten or fifteen years ago.

119
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:40,480
It feels very like physical and tactile, and there's a lot of like it's intuitive in the way that a physical object is intuitive, if that makes sense.

120
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:52,720
Like your tabs look like paper tabs with, you know, depth and shading, and all of your different themes are not just sets of colors, but like there's actual textures and everything that goes with those.

