00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:43,920
And one thing like we've found in like our consulting at least is doing rough sketches.

241
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:59,920
And in fact, even if we make a higher fidelity wireframe, sometimes we will intentionally lower that fidelity, like make it gray scale and take away elements because sometimes you're trying to show like the way a navigation flow feels or something like that.

242
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:15,040
And having those, like having colors or like specific details in there would distract from the actual conversation that needed to happen, which is like, should this, you know, back button work this way or should clicking this take you over to this spot?

243
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:17,840
And it's not as important what the back button looks like right now.

244
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:25,040
And so it was almost like a way to trick your brain into focusing on the actual problem you're trying to solve.

245
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:33,360
