00:51:34,320 --> 00:52:58,640
And like that created a little dialogue and help me solve my problem really fast and so the next time I ran into one of those issues I was like well maybe I can try this again and it worked again and then that sort of all snowballed into this sort of Twitter actually using Twitter to use as my like coworkers I guess in some ways I really like the iOS development community on Twitter like it feels like a safe and welcoming place and I also like sharing like if I see like a newbie that has questions like I like retweeting it or sharing it or tagging someone that might be out of help because like I've received a lot of help and support from the community and like if I can boost someone else and get them the help they need that is a really great feeling yeah like that is one thing that I learned early on from you actually is reaching out to random people or letting random people sort of engage with you or whatever is extremely rewarding and like you you very quickly were like encouraging me with random little things i don't even remember i just remember like in my head you were this person who had released an app in the store, and so even though it was only a couple months removed from when I released something, it's, it's crazy how big of a gap that seems in your head.

